  {
   "id": "cap-bcl",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -900,
   "y": -1450,
   "width": 2600,
   "height": 64,
   "text": "routed experts 896×92 **48.62B** (46.7%) · KDA mixers ×69 **30.62B** (29.4%) · gated MLA ×24 **5.57B** (5.3%) · shared experts + router ×92 **12.75B** (12.2%) · latent down/up proj ×92 **4.73B** (4.5%) · dense FFN ×1 **726.7M** (0.7%) · lm head **1.17B** (1.1%) · embed **0** (row lookup) · vision tower + projector **0** (runs per image) · norms + AttnRes queries **4.0M** (<0.1%)"
  },
  {
   "id": "cap-title",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -900,
   "y": -1300,
   "width": 1250,
   "height": 200,
   "text": "# Kimi K3 — model  \nOne continuous decoder stack L0–92, read top → bottom; layers that repeat are drawn once with **×N**. **Grey bars = tensors**, length ∝ channels per token (0.08 px/channel). **Boxes = operations**, all one size; where parameters and compute live is the pair of bars above. T = sequence length. *Layer* tab = one decoder layer in detail."
  },
  {
   "id": "cap-legend",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 450,
   "y": -1300,
   "width": 1250,
   "height": 200,
   "text": "Row colours — **cyan: KDA** (Kimi Delta Attention, linear: fixed 96×128×128 state, no KV cache) ×69 · **orange: gated MLA** (full softmax attention, 96 heads, 512+64 latent KV cache, no RoPE) ×24. Pattern 3 KDA + 1 MLA, and the last two layers (L91, L92) are both MLA.    \nEvery layer but L0 is MoE: **16 of 896** routed experts in a 3584-dim latent space + 2 shared experts, sigmoid router. L0 has a dense FFN. Side boxes = **Attention-Residual blocks** of 12 layers."
  },
  {
   "id": "raw1",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -980,
   "width": 300,
   "height": 56,
   "text": "**raw text**  \"The cat sat…\"",
   "color": "#64748b"
  },
