   "x": -597,
   "y": 935,
   "width": 440,
   "height": 34,
   "text": "`x [T, 7168]`"
  },
  {
   "id": "head31",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 0,
   "y": 996,
   "width": 300,
   "height": 56,
   "text": "**lm head** — 7168 → 163840  \n1.17B · not tied to embed",
   "color": "2"
  },
  {
   "id": "logits32",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -750,
   "y": 1092,
   "width": 1800,
   "height": 9,
   "text": "",
   "color": "#64748b"
  },
  {
   "id": "note-lbl33",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -1210,
   "y": 1080,
   "width": 440,
   "height": 34,
   "text": "`logits [T, 163840]` — bar clipped (real 13107px)"
  },
  {
   "id": "samp34",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 0,
   "y": 1141,
   "width": 300,
   "height": 56,
   "text": "**softmax → sample**",
   "color": "#64748b"
  },
  {
   "id": "next35",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 0,
   "y": 1237,
   "width": 300,
   "height": 56,
   "text": "**next token id**",
   "color": "#64748b"
  },
  {
   "id": "note-attnres",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -1440,
   "y": -247,
   "width": 980,
   "height": 330,
   "text": "**Attention Residuals (AttnRes).** There is no plain residual stream. Layers are grouped in blocks of 12; each block's outputs are summed into a partial sum *s*, and the first layer of each block freezes the previous sum as a snapshot b (b0 = the embedding). Before its attention and again before its FFN, every layer feeds on a **softmax-weighted mix of all snapshots so far + s** (L0's attention reads the embedding directly) — weights from one learned 7168-vector (proj × RMSNorm weight) scored against each RMS-normalised candidate, per token. A layer *returns* s + its outputs, not x + outputs. 8 snapshots at the end; the output mix sees all 8 + s."
  },
  {
   "id": "note-mixers",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -1440,
   "y": 113,
   "width": 980,
   "height": 250,
   "text": "**Why mix KDA and MLA?** A KDA layer keeps one 128×128 matrix per head (96 heads = 1.57M values) that it decays per channel and updates token by token — cost per token is constant however long the context.    \nAn MLA layer caches a 512+64 = 576-value latent for every past token. At 1,048,576 tokens: 24 MLA layers ≈ **14.5G** cached values vs 69 KDA layers ≈ **109M** state values (constant)."
  },
  {
   "id": "note-nope",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -1440,
   "y": 393,
   "width": 980,
   "height": 200,
   "text": "**No positional encoding anywhere in the text model** (mla_use_nope, no rotary weights or calls). Order comes from the KDA layers: a causal 4-tap conv on q/k/v and the recurrence itself. MLA keeps DeepSeek's split (128 + 64 dims per head, the 64 shared across heads) but never rotates it. Context 1,048,576 positions."
  },
  {
   "id": "note-moe",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 540,
   "y": 13,
   "width": 760,
   "height": 300,
   "text": "**Latent MoE.** Routed experts don't see the 7168-wide hidden state: one down-proj squeezes it to 3584, the 16 chosen experts (each SiTU-GLU 3584→3072→3584, 33.0M) work there, then RMSNorm + up-proj back to 7168. This halves every expert. The 2 shared experts (one SiTU-GLU 7168→6144→7168) and the router stay full width. Expert weights are MXFP4 (4-bit, one shared exponent per 32 weights); everything else BF16."
  },
  {
   "id": "note-situ",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 540,
   "y": 343,
   "width": 760,
   "height": 180,
   "text": "**SiTU-GLU** (every FFN): out = β·tanh(g/β)·σ(g) · β'·tanh(u/β') with g = gate, u = up, β = 4, β' = 25 — a SiLU-like gate with both branches soft-clipped."
  },
  {
   "id": "note-src",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -900,
   "y": 1373,
   "width": 1300,
   "height": 170,
   "text": "**Sources.** config.json + safetensors headers of moonshotai/Kimi-K3 (497,220 tensors). Text model (L0–92, embed, head) = **2779.48B**, + 447.4M vision. Routed experts are MXFP4 packed 2 per byte (counted ×2; U8 scales not counted). Dataflow from the repo's modeling_kimi_linear.py and modeling_kimi_k3.py. No MTP / draft head in the checkpoint."
  }
 ],
